# Twenty CRM SSO (do not regress)

Clicking **CRM** must stay on the Flolah CRM page in an **iframe**, same as **ERP**. Do not `window.location.replace` the Flolah tab onto Twenty.

## Required flow

1. Server mints a Twenty LOGIN JWT and **exchanges it server-side** (`getAuthTokensFromLoginToken` on the **company workspace origin** `{sub}.crm.<apex>` — not apex `crm.<apex>`).
2. Persist the exchanged pair; iframe gets a **short apply token** `t=` (no JWT in the URL).
3. Iframe loads `{sub}.crm.<apex>/flolah-handoff/?owner=&wipe=1&t=` → `/flolah-crm-sso` writes `tokenPairState` / `tokenPair` (and dual Partitioned cookies like ERP, without a huge `tokenPair` JSON Set-Cookie) then `location.replace("/")` **inside the iframe**.
4. Flolah chrome (Sync org / Open in new tab / Workspace) stays around the iframe.

## Never do this

- Send the iframe or window to Twenty `/verify?loginToken=` (Authentication failed → `/welcome`).
- Nest `/verify?loginToken=` inside another query (browsers split on `?`).
- Navigate the **Flolah window** to the CRM host (breaks the iframe shell users already have).
- `Set-Cookie` the full Twenty tokenPair JSON (nginx 502: upstream sent too big header).
- Trust body `ceo_user_id` / workspace ids for authorization.

## After changing SSO

- Update `knowledgebase/platform-help/32-business-core-crm-erp.md`, `docs-site/docs/systems/crm-and-erp.md`, `deploy/business-core/README.md`.
- Keep `backend/scripts/test-twenty-sso-handoff.js` and `vps-verify-crm-sso.js` asserting `t=` and **no** `loginToken` / `/verify`.
- Deploy via `sync-to-vps.ps1` (frontend + backend). No VPS hotfixes.
